    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1587">

                <pb facs="1329" n="1225" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg1225"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 723.2515/272.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Minister to
                        Peru.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-11-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Nov. 12, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Department has been informed by Legation at Santiago and Chilean Minister
                    here that an agreement has been effected for reestablishment of diplomatic
                    relations between Peru and Chile and the settlement of Tacna-Arica question. Has
                    Peruvian Government officially informed you of the conclusion of such an
                    arrangement so full of promise for the future welfare of both countries? What
                    are the probabilities for its ratification by Peruvian Congress?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
